# tally 2.2.1 P50 B3 (O §2.2: "Inputs. As run"): reprint reads --pin=bytes: a member pinned by its
# canonical hash is LOAD-PIN under it (review g4 findings/b3). Before W13: the pin ignored.
=== options reprint pin=bytes exit=1
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-04-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-06-30

source s "s"
input one: int

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  one = 1

ask q: one
=== top_canon.tally
model fam
  tally 2
  on 2026-04-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-06-30
  use a = "m.tally" sha256 "8c9f5e28182b6f1df62eceb9c0dcb5c9c69f4baa423dc53157066792628dc7ca"
=== expect
refused: LOAD-PIN m.tally doesn't match its sha256 in use a
